<div id="header">
  Category: Post-doc advanced research project (Babes-Bolyai University)
  coupled with POCU: antrepreneurship and innovation
</div>
    
<div id="content">

  <p align="center"><img src="pocu/pocu-scheme.png" width="600" height="auto"></p>
  <br>

<h3>Valorisation of astaxanthin derived from waste crab shells recovered by low-footprint and low-cost method</h3>
<br>
    <h4><b>Funder:</b> Babes&#791-Bolyai University and the European Social Fund, through the project POCU: Antrepreneurship and innovation in doctoral and postdoctoral research</h4>
    <h4><b>Competition:</b>Group III recruitment competition within project POCU 123886</h4>
    <h4><b>Duration:</b> antrepreneurial education 1.5.2021-1.5.2022; research project - ongoing<h4>
	<h4><b>Function: Principal investigator (scientific part); participant - postdoctoral student (antrepreneurial part)</h4>
  
 <h3>Project scope (scientific part)</h3>
    <p align="justify">Astaxanthin is a carotenoid known for its antioxidative 
	capacity, which may reach up to 100 times higher than tocopherol. It is 
	being incorporated in numerous nutritional supplements and animal feed. 
	Astaxanthin attached a particular research interest in the fields of 
	spectroscopy, nutrition and nanomedicine.</p>
	<br>
	<p>This project aims to develop a cheap an effective method for obtaining 
	and re-utilization astaxanthin-rich extracts from waste biogenic materials 
	leftover from crustaceans industrial exploitation. Am optimised extraction 
	procedure will be developed for further use not only the valuable carotenoid, 
	but also the porous biogenic matrix relying on Mg-calcite mineral on 
	chitin-protein scaffold. Finally, a formulation of the purified astaxanthin 
	into usable solutions, aggregates and tablets will be proposed, as added-value 
	products from waste. The project goal is to develop a robust, inexpensive
	and sustainable procedure for extraction and purification of astaxanthin from 
	crab shells as an added-value by-product.</p>
   
  	   <p align="center"><img src="pocu/pocu-scheme-2.png" width="400" height="auto"></p>
       <br>
	   
	   <h3>Objectives</h3>
	   <p><b>Aim:</b> Develop a robust, inexpensive and sustainable procedure for extraction and purification of astaxanthin from crab shells (seafood waste) as an added-value by-product. Formulate astaxanthin products as 1) solution, 2) aggregates, 3) in solid state (pressed into a tablet).</li>
	    <ol>
	      <li>Optimization of astaxanthin extraction from the waste crab shells.)</li>
          <li>Purification of extracted astaxanthin</p>
          <li>Establishing astaxanthin-containing products</li>
		  <li>Knowledge dissemination.</li>
		</ol>
	  <br>
  <h3>Achievements</h3>
          <ul>
		    <li><b>Accumulated knowledge base</b> on existing extraction methods of carotenoids from crustacean shells, their advantages and drawbacks.</li>
			<li><b>Method established</b> for efficient carotenoids extraction using acetone.</li>	
            <li><b>method established</b> for purification of carotenoids based on solvent-solvent extraction and preparative HPLC.</a>.</li>
		  </ul>
  
